**4. Platform Architecture**

**Multi-Tenant Architecture**

\[PLATFORM NAME\] is built on a hybrid multi-tenant SaaS architecture.
All tenants share the same application infrastructure and codebase,
while data is logically isolated per tenant through strict tenant_id
scoping at every layer of the data model. This approach provides the
scalability of shared infrastructure while ensuring complete data
separation between companies.

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Layer**          **Approach**          **Notes**
  ------------------ --------------------- ------------------------------
  Application / API  Shared                Single codebase; all tenants
                                           served from same application

  Database           Shared schema,        Every record includes
                     isolated data         tenant_id; row-level security
                                           enforced

  File / Document    Isolated per tenant   Separate storage buckets or
  Storage                                  folder namespacing per tenant

  Authentication     Tenant-scoped         Users belong to exactly one
                                           tenant; no cross-tenant login

  Configuration      Per-tenant            Branding, workflow settings,
                                           custom fields per tenant

  Encryption         Per-tenant keys       Sensitive financial and PII
                                           data encrypted with
                                           tenant-specific keys

  Rate Limiting      Per-tenant            Heavy tenants cannot degrade
                                           performance for others
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**Three-Tier Platform Model**

**Tier 1 --- Enterprise (Company Level)**

The highest level of the platform. Manages the entire business across
all active projects. Includes company profile, user management,
cross-project dashboards, financial reporting, resource management,
vendor database, compliance tracking, and accounting integration.

**Tier 2 --- Project Level**

Each job gets a dedicated project environment. Includes scheduling
(Gantt), budget tracking, document management, RFIs, submittals, change
orders, inspections, subcontractor management, AIA billing, lien waiver
tracking, and the client-facing portal.

**Tier 3 --- Trade / Task Level**

The deepest level --- trade-specific workflows, phase gates, checklists,
material tracking, and inspection records tailored to each discipline.
This is the core differentiator of the platform. Each trade module is
built to reflect how that trade actually operates.

**Super Admin Layer**

A separate administrative console above all tenant environments,
accessible only to \[PLATFORM NAME\] platform operators. Provides tenant
provisioning and deactivation, subscription and billing management,
platform-wide feature flag control, usage analytics, global template
library management, read-only tenant impersonation for support,
infrastructure health monitoring, and audit logging.

**Cross-Tenant Collaboration Architecture**

When a General Contractor (Tenant A) awards a scope of work to a
Subcontractor (Tenant B), both parties may be independent tenants on the
platform. The cross-tenant collaboration feature creates a governed
Shared Project Layer --- a controlled data bridge between the two
tenants --- exposing only the data relevant to their joint scope.

Key design principles of the Shared Project Layer:

-   Neither tenant gains access to the other\'s internal company data

-   Data sharing is governed by explicit permission tables per
    connection

-   Either party may disconnect at project closeout, archiving the
    shared record for both

-   A sub may be simultaneously connected to multiple GC tenants across
    different projects

-   Non-tenant subcontractors (not yet subscribers) receive a limited
    free portal to prevent GC adoption blockers

**5. User Roles & Permissions**

Access control is enforced at both the tenant level and the role level.
Every user belongs to exactly one tenant. Permissions are role-based and
configurable by tenant administrators within the bounds of their
subscription tier.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Role**         **Scope**          **Key Permissions**
  ---------------- ------------------ ---------------------------------------
  Owner / Admin    Full company       All access --- users, financials,
                                      settings, all projects, billing

  Project Manager  Assigned projects  Full project control --- schedule,
                                      budget, docs, change orders, subs

  Estimator        Pre-construction   Estimating, bidding, takeoffs, bid
                                      leveling --- no field access

  Foreman /        Assigned projects  Field reports, schedules, crew
  Superintendent                      management, task completion, photos

  Field Technician Own tasks only     Clock in/out, task completion, photo
                                      uploads, daily reports

  Subcontractor    Assigned scope     Submittals, task status, invoice
  (External)       only               submission, RFI response

  Client           Portal only        Project progress, photos, change order
                                      approval, invoice approval

  Accountant       Financial data     Job costing, invoices, QuickBooks sync,
                   only               financial reports

  Safety Officer   All projects       Safety reports, incident logs,
                   (safety)           compliance checklists
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

**Permission Categories**

-   View --- read-only access to data

-   Edit --- create and modify records

-   Approve --- formal approval workflows (change orders, invoices,
    submittals)

-   Delete --- remove records (restricted to Admin and PM by default)

-   Financial --- access to cost data, budgets, and invoices (restricted
    by role)

-   Export --- ability to export data and generate reports

