**9. Mobile Application Requirements**

The mobile application is a first-class product --- not a stripped-down
version of the web platform. Field use is the primary use case, and the
mobile app is the primary touchpoint for foremen and field technicians.
All critical field functions must be available on mobile with a native,
fast, intuitive experience.

**Platform Requirements**

-   iOS (iPhone and iPad) --- iOS 16 and above

-   Android --- Android 11 and above

-   Offline mode: all critical field functions available without
    internet connectivity

-   Automatic background sync when connectivity is restored

-   Push notifications for schedule changes, approvals, RFI responses,
    and inspection results

**Core Mobile Features**

**Time & Attendance**

-   GPS-verified clock in and clock out per job site

-   Geofence alert if clock-in location does not match job site

-   Break tracking

-   Crew clock-in --- foreman can clock in multiple crew members
    simultaneously

-   Weekly hours summary per employee

**Daily Field Reports**

-   Voice-to-text notes for faster entry in the field

-   Crew count entry with manpower hours

-   Work performed description by trade/area

-   Material deliveries received with quantity and supplier

-   Equipment on site log

-   Visitor and inspection log

-   Weather conditions auto-populated via GPS location

-   Photo attachment with automatic GPS and timestamp

**Task Management**

-   View assigned tasks for the day and week

-   Mark tasks complete with optional photo proof

-   Create tasks and assign to crew members

-   View trade-specific phase checklist items

**Document & Plan Viewer**

-   Full plan set viewer with pinch-to-zoom

-   Drawing markup and annotation tools in field

-   RFI creation from a markup on a drawing

-   Offline plan caching --- plans downloaded for offline access

-   Always loads latest approved revision automatically

**Inspections**

-   Inspection checklist completion in field

-   Pass/fail entry with notes

-   Photo documentation attached per checklist item

-   Automatic notification to PM on inspection completion or failure

**Safety**

-   Safety incident report creation

-   Near-miss reporting

-   Toolbox talk sign-off with digital crew signatures

-   Photo documentation of hazards

**Material & Delivery Tracking**

-   Scan or photograph delivery tickets

-   Confirm material receipt against purchase orders

-   Flag short shipments or damaged materials

