**QuickBooks Integration --- Detail**

QuickBooks is the primary integration and a key purchase driver. The
integration must support:

-   Bi-directional sync of customers, vendors, and chart of accounts

-   Automatic creation of invoices in QuickBooks when a draw is approved
    in the platform

-   Expense and bill sync to job cost categories

-   Payroll hours export to QuickBooks Payroll or ADP

-   Bank reconciliation-ready reporting

-   Class tracking mapped to project/job codes

-   Sub-customer hierarchy for project-level P&L in QuickBooks

**11. Non-Functional Requirements**

**11.1 Performance**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Requirement**                     **Target**
  ----------------------------------- -----------------------------------
  Page load time (web app)            \< 2 seconds for all primary
                                      screens

  Mobile app launch time              \< 3 seconds cold start

  API response time (P95)             \< 500ms for standard queries

  Plan viewer load (large file set)   \< 5 seconds for initial render

  File upload (documents/photos)      Resumable uploads; 100MB max per
                                      file

  Concurrent users per tenant         Support 500+ concurrent users at
                                      Business/Enterprise tier

  Report generation                   \< 10 seconds for standard reports;
                                      async for large exports
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**11.2 Security**

-   SOC 2 Type II compliance roadmap (target: 18 months post-launch)

-   TLS 1.3 encryption for all data in transit

-   AES-256 encryption for all data at rest

-   Tenant-level encryption key management for sensitive data

-   Multi-factor authentication (MFA) option for all users; enforceable
    by tenant admin

-   Role-based access control enforced at API layer --- no client-side
    permission bypass possible

-   Complete tenant data isolation --- row-level security on all
    database queries

-   Regular penetration testing (quarterly)

-   Vulnerability disclosure policy and bug bounty program

-   GDPR-ready data handling for future international expansion

**11.3 Reliability & Availability**

-   99.9% uptime SLA for Business and Enterprise tiers

-   99.5% uptime SLA for Starter and Professional tiers

-   Automated daily backups with 30-day retention

-   Point-in-time recovery capability

-   Multi-region failover for database and file storage

-   Incident status page with real-time updates

**11.4 Scalability**

-   Horizontal scaling of application tier --- auto-scaling based on
    load

-   Database read replicas for reporting and analytics workloads

-   CDN delivery for all static assets and plan files

-   Tenant-aware rate limiting to prevent noisy-neighbor degradation

-   Architecture supports migration of high-volume tenants to dedicated
    infrastructure

**11.5 Data & Privacy**

-   Tenant data export available on demand (full JSON/CSV export)

-   Data deletion workflow on tenant cancellation (30-day grace period,
    then purge)

-   Personally identifiable information (PII) handling policy

-   Document retention configurable per tenant

**12. Subscription Tiers & Pricing**

**Pricing Philosophy**

Tiers are structured around company scale and operational complexity ---
not contractor type. A masonry company, an electrical contractor, and a
general contractor with the same team size and project volume belong on
the same tier. What differs is which trade modules and optional features
they activate. Every tier is fully trade-neutral at onboarding: the
company selects their trade type and the platform configures their
default modules accordingly.

The GC module is not assumed or forced on any tenant. It is an optional
activation available from the Business tier upward, or available as a
paid add-on for Professional tier companies that occasionally perform
general contracting work.

