**Appendix A --- Glossary**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Term**           **Definition**
  ------------------ ----------------------------------------------------
  Tenant             A subscribing company on the platform --- has its
                     own isolated data environment

  Multi-Tenant       Architecture where multiple companies share the same
                     platform infrastructure with isolated data

  Cross-Tenant       Feature enabling two separate tenants (GC and Sub)
  Collaboration      to share project data through a governed bridge

  Trade Module       A discipline-specific feature set with phase gates,
                     checklists, and data fields for one construction
                     trade

  Shared Project     The controlled data bridge between two connected
  Layer              tenants on a shared project

  AIA Billing        American Institute of Architects standard billing
                     format (G702/G703) for progress billing on
                     construction projects

  CSI Division       Construction Specifications Institute numbering
                     system for organizing construction work by category

  Lien Waiver        Legal document releasing a party\'s right to file a
                     mechanic\'s lien against a property

  Preliminary Notice Legal notice required in many states to preserve
                     lien rights before work begins

  GMP                Guaranteed Maximum Price --- contract type where the
                     contractor assumes risk for cost overruns above a
                     ceiling

  Davis-Bacon        Federal law requiring prevailing wage rates on
                     public construction projects, requiring certified
                     payroll

  RFI                Request for Information --- formal document
                     requesting clarification from the design team

  Submittal          Material or shop drawing submitted by a contractor
                     for design team review and approval

  COI                Certificate of Insurance --- document verifying a
                     subcontractor\'s insurance coverage

  TAB                Test, Adjust, and Balance --- HVAC commissioning
                     process verifying airflow and system performance

  AFCI / GFCI        Arc Fault Circuit Interrupter / Ground Fault Circuit
                     Interrupter --- electrical safety devices required
                     by code

  MRR                Monthly Recurring Revenue --- primary SaaS business
                     metric

  CAGR               Compound Annual Growth Rate --- measure of market or
                     revenue growth over time
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**12. Internationalization & Localization**

Multilingual support is not a feature --- it is a foundational product
requirement. The US construction workforce is 31% Hispanic/Latino (2024
BLS/CPWR data), a share growing every year. In New York City, Spanish is
now spoken by 39.3% of construction workers --- nearly matching English
at 40.1%. In Texas, California, and Florida combined, over 834,000 +
808,000 + 317,000 Hispanic construction workers represent more than half
the national Hispanic construction workforce. A platform that doesn\'t
speak Spanish cannot serve this industry.

> **Safety Imperative:**
>
> This is not only a market access issue --- it is a safety and
> liability issue. The National Safety Council documents a 25% reduction
> in jobsite incidents at companies offering multilingual safety
> training. Inspection result notifications, safety warnings, and
> compliance documents sent in a language workers cannot read create
> direct legal exposure. Spanish support in v1.0 is mandatory, not
> optional.

