  Required**   Spanish (ES)                Hispanic/Latino. In NYC Spanish
                                           matches English nearly 1:1 (39.3% vs
                                           40.1%). TX, CA, FL hold 50%+ of the
                                           Hispanic construction workforce.

  **Tier 2 --- Portuguese ---  v1.1        1.8% of foreign-born construction
  High         Brazilian                   workers. Major concentrations in
  Priority**   (PT-BR)                     Greater Boston, Miami, New Jersey,
                                           Texas. Brazilian construction crews
                                           are a well-documented regional
                                           workforce.

  **Tier 2 --- Haitian Creole  v1.1        Significant workforce in Florida
  High         (HT)                        (Miami), New York, Boston.
  Priority**                               Explicitly added to US Dept of
                                           Labor\'s MigrantWorker.gov as a
                                           priority construction language.

  **Tier 3 --- Polish (PL) +   v2.0        Polish: 1.5% of foreign-born
  Planned**    Ukrainian (UK)              construction workers --- heavy
                                           Midwest presence (Chicago, Detroit).
                                           Ukrainian: surged post-2022
                                           invasion; concentrated Northeast +
                                           Midwest.

  **Tier 3 --- Vietnamese (VI) v2.0        Gulf Coast (Houston, New Orleans),
  Planned**                                California, Pacific Northwest.
                                           Notably strong in framing and
