**12.3 Technical i18n Requirements**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Requirement**     **Specification**
  ------------------- ---------------------------------------------------
  i18n library        react-i18next --- shared across React web app and
                      React Native mobile app. Consistent translation key
                      namespace across platforms.

  Translation file    JSON files organized by namespace --- one namespace
  format              per major feature area (e.g. schedule.json,
                      financials.json, field.json, common.json).
                      Namespaced to prevent key collisions and enable
                      lazy loading.

  Locale detection    Browser Accept-Language header → user account
  --- web             preferred_language setting → tenant
                      default_language → EN fallback.

  Locale detection    Device system locale → user account
  --- mobile          preferred_language → EN fallback. User can override
                      in Profile settings.

  Date / time         Intl.DateTimeFormat API throughout --- never
  formatting          hardcoded date strings. Locale-aware: MM/DD/YYYY
                      (en-US), DD/MM/YYYY (es, pt-BR).

  Number / currency   Intl.NumberFormat API --- currency amounts always
  formatting          in locale format. Amounts in cents on the wire;
                      formatted for display per locale.

  String length       Spanish and Portuguese strings are typically 20-30%
  accommodation       longer than English equivalents. All UI components
                      must be tested with ES strings --- no truncation of
                      critical labels.

  Pluralization       react-i18next i18nPlurals --- handles irregular
                      plurals per language (English: 1 item / 2 items;
                      Spanish: 1 elemento / 2 elementos).

  RTL preparation     Arabic (Tier 4) requires right-to-left layout. CSS
                      logical properties (margin-inline-start instead of
                      margin-left) used throughout from v1.0 so RTL is an
                      enablement, not a rebuild.

  Translation         Phrase, Lokalise, or Crowdin (TBD) as translation
  management          management platform. Professional translators for
                      all Tier 1 and Tier 2 content --- no machine
                      translation for safety-critical text.

  Missing translation EN fallback for any untranslated key --- never
  fallback            display a raw key string to users.
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**12.4 Translation Workflow**

-   All user-facing strings defined in English source files first --- no
    hardcoded strings in component code

-   Phrase/Lokalise integrated with GitHub --- new keys auto-flagged for
    translation on PR merge

-   Professional human translators for all safety-related strings, legal
    terminology, and field-worker-facing UI

-   Machine translation (DeepL) acceptable for internal admin screens
    and low-risk UI copy, reviewed before shipping

-   Native speaker QA for each language before release --- a bilingual
    construction professional, not just a language translator

-   Spanish translation complete and QA-passed as a v1.0 launch gate ---
    no exceptions
